# Queue jobs (BullMQ on Redis)

- Every job is idempotent: running it twice with the same payload has the same result.
- Payloads carry IDs and small params, never full objects or large text.
- Use explicit `jobId` for dedupe where a job must not be enqueued twice.
- Configure `attempts` + exponential backoff; permanently failed jobs are kept for inspection.
- External calls (job sources, LLM) have timeouts and per-source rate limits in Redis.
- One processor per file: `<queue-name>.processor.ts`, logic delegated to a service.
- Log job id, queue, attempt, and duration on completion and failure.
